claimed: intent-model-persistence — request 4 of seven from the consumer, and the piece that makes "no generation on the request path" also mean "no FITTING on the request path". Trained is arrays of doubles with no codec, so fitting lives wherever loading lives: every process start re-fits, and re-fitting needs the teacher, which drags an embedding server into the STARTUP path even when the request path is clean. Give Probe.Trained, Centroid.Trained, CharGrams.Trained, Static.Table and NoModel.Trained a Schema so a model is data -- fitted at build time, loaded at boot. Two things to get right rather than assume: the weights are Array[Double] and Embedding is ArraySeq[Float], neither of which the derivation handles by default, and SBytes exists precisely because an embedding once travelled as List[Double]; and a loaded model must be VERIFIABLY the same classifier, which is a round-trip property test rather than a hope.
